                <pb facs="0669" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg573"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">memorandum.</hi></head>
                <p>Mr. Kelting is the bookkeeper and Spanish translator for George D. Emery, of
                    Boston, Mass., who has a mahogany-cutting concession on the Atlantic coast of
                    Nicaragua, with fifteen years to run. Mr. Kelting is a German citizen and a man
                    of excellent reputation. Mr. Emery pays the Nicaraguan Government $10,000 gold
                    per annum bonus and $1 on each mahogany log exported, amounting to over $15,000
                    per annum exclusive of the bonus above stated, and gives permanent employment to
                    about 150 Americans besides about 500 natives.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. L. M.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
